# Assistant unit design (non-authoritative)

This tree closes practical gaps in the NASA-V **unit design** phase so unit testing can proceed even though authoritative `docs/design/` is incomplete.

**Not authoritative.** Root docs and `docs/design/` win on conflict. These files only answer questions the authoritative unit docs leave open, or cover units that have no authoritative unit doc yet.

## Conventions

- **Inferred** — forced by authoritative text or by decisions already recorded under `decisions.md`.
- **Assumed** — picked so work can proceed; veto-friendly. Prefer searching `assumed` when reviewing.
- Stable ids look like `UD-SHADE-1` so tests and notes can cite a single point of change.
- Stay in the unit-design lane: behaviors, actors, relations, responsibilities — not implementation trivia.

## Layout

- `decisions.md` — developer rulings from the Q&A pass (source of truth for this tree)
- `coverage-matrix.md` — architecture + requirements → unit coverage
- `supplements/` — one file per existing `docs/design/*.md` (same basename)
- `new/` — unit designs for units with no authoritative design file

## How to use

1. Read the matching authoritative design first (if any).
2. Read the supplement or `new/` file for gaps.
3. Treat `assumed` entries as provisional until confirmed or replaced in authoritative docs.
